.TH EUCLID-CLI-EQS 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eqs \- manage Euclid SQS-compatible queues and messages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli
[\fB\-\-endpoint\fR \fIURL\fR]
[\fB\-\-loglevel\fR \fILEVEL\fR]
.B eqs
.I action
[\fIaction-options\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B eqs
module talks to the Euclid gateway's eqs service to create and manage
SQS-compatible queues and their messages. Every
.B eqs
command sends a single JSON request to the gateway
(\fB\-\-endpoint\fR, default \fIhttps://localhost:5566\fR) and prints the
JSON response on success.
.PP
All
.B eqs
commands require the caller to be authenticated; see
.B AUTHENTICATION
below for how the session used to sign these requests is obtained.
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
.B create-queue
Creates a new queue, optionally with a dead letter queue, visibility
timeout, retry limit, message size limit and delivery delay. See
.BR euclid-cli-eqs-create-queue (1).
.TP
.B list-queues
Lists queues, optionally filtered by name prefix, paged and sorted. See
.BR euclid-cli-eqs-list-queues (1).
.TP
.B get-queue-ern
Resolves a queue's Euclid resource name (ERN) by its name. See
.BR euclid-cli-eqs-get-queue-ern (1).
.TP
.B get-queue-metadata
Shows a queue's metadata (region, account, namespace, size, message
counts). See
.BR euclid-cli-eqs-get-queue-metadata (1).
.TP
.B delete-queue
Deletes a queue by its ERN. See
.BR euclid-cli-eqs-delete-queue (1).
.TP
.B purge-queue
Deletes all messages from a single queue. See
.BR euclid-cli-eqs-purge-queue (1).
.TP
.B purge-all-queues
Deletes all messages from every queue in a region/account. See
.BR euclid-cli-eqs-purge-all-queues (1).
.TP
.B send-message
Sends a message to a queue, with optional attributes and priority. See
.BR euclid-cli-eqs-send-message (1).
.TP
.B receive-messages
Receives up to a given number of messages from a queue, favoring higher
priority messages. See
.BR euclid-cli-eqs-receive-messages (1).
.TP
.B list-messages
Lists a queue's messages without receiving them, i.e. without changing
their status or visibility. See
.BR euclid-cli-eqs-list-messages (1).
.TP
.B set-visibility
Sets the visibility timeout for an individual message. See
.BR euclid-cli-eqs-set-visibility (1).
.TP
.B get-message-count
Returns a queue's message counters (total, invisible, delayed). See
.BR euclid-cli-eqs-get-message-count (1).
.TP
.B get-message-attribute
Returns a single message attribute by name. See
.BR euclid-cli-eqs-get-message-attribute (1).
.TP
.B get-message-metadata
Shows a single message's metadata (status, priority, size, receive
count, timestamps, etc.). See
.BR euclid-cli-eqs-get-message-metadata (1).
.TP
.B set-message-attribute
Sets the value of a single message attribute, creating it if it doesn't
exist yet. See
.BR euclid-cli-eqs-set-message-attribute (1).
.TP
.B add-queue-tag
Adds a tag to a queue. See
.BR euclid-cli-eqs-add-queue-tag (1).
.TP
.B set-queue-tag
Sets the value of an existing queue tag. See
.BR euclid-cli-eqs-set-queue-tag (1).
.TP
.B delete-queue-tag
Deletes a tag from a queue. See
.BR euclid-cli-eqs-delete-queue-tag (1).
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
These options are given to
.B euclid-cli
itself, before the
.I eqs
module name.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-endpoint " " \fIURL\fR
Euclid gateway endpoint to talk to, e.g. \fIhttps://localhost:5566\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-ca\-cert " " \fIPATH\fR
Path to a PEM CA certificate to trust in addition to the system trust
store, e.g. for self-signed development certificates.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
Path to a JSON configuration file providing defaults for action
options (currently used by
.BR euclid-cli-esm (1)
only). Defaults to
.IR /usr/local/euclid/etc/euclid.json ;
silently ignored if the file doesn't exist.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-signature " " \fISCHEME\fR
Signature scheme used for signed service calls: \fIsigv4\fR (the
default) or \fIrfc9421\fR for RFC 9421 HTTP Message Signatures. Both
prove the request with the same access key; RFC 9421 puts the
signature in \fISignature\fR/\fISignature\-Input\fR headers and binds
the body through \fIContent\-Digest\fR (RFC 9530) instead of using
AWS's Authorization header. Overrides
.I euclid.cli.signature
from the configuration file. Ignored for
.BR euclid-cli-eam (1)
commands, which authenticate with the session's bearer token.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-loglevel " " \fILEVEL\fR
Log level: one of \fItrace\fR, \fIdebug\fR, \fIinfo\fR, \fIwarning\fR,
\fIerror\fR, \fIfatal\fR. Defaults to \fIinfo\fR.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print top-level usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the euclid-cli version and exit.
.SH AUTHENTICATION
.B eqs
commands are authenticated using the session created by
.BR euclid-cli-eam-login (1),
loaded from
.IR $HOME/.euclid/credentials .
Unlike
.B eam
commands, which always send the bearer token,
.B eqs
requests are signed with SigV4 (the same scheme Euclid SDKs use for SQS)
using the access key ID and secret stored in that file, if present;
.BR euclid-cli-eam-login (1)
provisions this access key automatically on first login, so a separate
.B eam create-access-key
call is not normally needed. If no access key is stored, the bearer
token is sent instead as an
.I "Authorization: Bearer"
header.
.PP
If the server rejects a request with
.IR "HTTP 401" ,
the stored credentials are left untouched (unlike
.BR eam ,
which clears them on 401); run
.B euclid-cli eam login
again if requests start failing with 401.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The action completed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
Argument parsing failed, the request could not be sent, or the server
rejected it (missing/expired session, invalid input, queue or message
not found, etc.). Details are printed to standard error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $HOME/.euclid/credentials
JSON file holding the current session's bearer token and/or SigV4
access key, created by
.B euclid-cli eam login
and read by every
.B eqs
action.
.SH EXAMPLES
Create a queue, resolve its ERN, and send/receive a message:
.PP
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eqs create-queue \e
    --name orders --visibility 30 --max-retries 3

euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eqs get-queue-ern \e
    --name orders

euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eqs send-message \e
    --ern ern:queues:eu-central-1:000000000000:queue:orders --body 'hello'

euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eqs receive-messages \e
    --ern ern:queues:eu-central-1:000000000000:queue:orders
.fi
.RE
.PP
Purge and delete a queue:
.PP
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eqs purge-queue \e
    --ern ern:queues:eu-central-1:000000000000:queue:orders

euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eqs delete-queue \e
    --ern ern:queues:eu-central-1:000000000000:queue:orders
.fi
.RE
